now that the line passes through the points $P(-1,4,5)$ and $Q(7,-1,2).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-1,2⟩-⟨-1,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,-5,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}.\n$$" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343559 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343560 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343561 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343562 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343563 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1041 "selection" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343562 13194139535319 true] [17592186343558 1110 #uuid "8b8616c8-9d1c-5552-be85-685b70032d50" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343559 1034 "\\frac{x+1}{-8}=\\frac{y-4}{-3}=\\frac{z-5}{-5}" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343559 1111 #uuid "12f09e9e-3f23-5403-911e-738d2b9c46bb" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343560 1034 "\\frac{x+1}{8}=\\frac{y+4}{-5}=\\frac{z+5}{-3}" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343560 1111 #uuid "bc74b0cd-f228-5745-8402-f886f256fcfc" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343561 1034 "\\frac{x+1}{-8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{3}" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343561 1111 #uuid "29c345eb-080c-5d4d-8336-39f30eeb7f6a" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343562 1034 "\\frac{x+1}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343562 1111 #uuid "212c1a75-9740-5370-b2ac-d752a8080b74" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343563 1034 "\\frac{x-1}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{5}=\\frac{z+5}{-3}" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343563 1111 #uuid "806ffd2b-5edb-58f0-801b-10e7ccac1f4b" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343564 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343565 13194139535319 true] [17592186343564 1089 "q-127527" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343564 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535319 true] [17592186343564 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/assets/8722b93655e069e2f35147b572c16ed7af408a86f8a88597c79aea8fe59e9c4d.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." 13194139535319 true] [17592186343564 1113 #uuid "660620a9-8a2e-5788-8e01-c31fb36aca66" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343564 1145 "We know that the line passes through the points $P(2,-1,3)$ and $Q(4,-3,3).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-3,3⟩-⟨2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{-2}=\\frac{z-3}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{-2}=\\frac{z-3}{0}.\n$$\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because $\\frac{z-3}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=3.$ For example, our two points $P(2,-1,3)$ and $Q(4,-3,3)$ both have $z$-coordinates of $z=3.$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-3}{0}$ part and instead write $z=3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{-2},\\,z=3.\n$$" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343566 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343567 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343568 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343569 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343570 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1041 "selection" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343569 13194139535319 true] [17592186343565 1110 #uuid "61f89ed3-9f36-5ed7-a075-840c44199506" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343566 1034 "\\frac{x-2}{-2}=\\frac{y+1}{4},\\,z=3" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343566 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343566 1111 #uuid "9640fe34-6da0-52cf-9be1-a13d9cbccd0f" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343567 1034 "\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y-1}{-4},\\,z=-3" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343567 1111 #uuid "155e553b-f3f1-523a-ba0f-6a59dc2489d7" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343568 1034 "\\frac{x-2}{-2}=\\frac{y+1}{-4},\\,z=-3" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343568 1111 #uuid "3a979667-d100-5f70-aaec-f521fe120305" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343569 1034 "\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{-2},\\,z=3" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343569 1111 #uuid "28d38cad-94b5-5266-8b60-2ced65e75903" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343570 1034 "\\frac{x+2}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{4},\\,z=3" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535319 true] [17592186343570 1111 #uuid "5466bdda-44a7-522d-ac23-7fefa26806d5" 13194139535319 true] [17592186343571 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343572 13194139535319 true] [17592186343571 1089 "q-71035" 131941395353